<title>BELGIUM: EU says Canadian wheat import tender opens on Friday.</title>
<headline>EU says Canadian wheat import tender opens on Friday.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Traders will be able to start bidding on Friday for licences to import 200,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat at a zero tariff, the European Union Official Journal said.</p>
<p>The concession covers 100,000 tonnes of durum wheat and 100,000 tonnes of quality common wheat. It is the first tranche of a 300,000 tonnes quota.</p>
<p>The second tranche is expected to be opened in the second half of 1997, a Commission official said.</p>
<p>Although the quota applies to wheat of any origin, it is intended to compensate Canada for export losses following Austrian, Swedish and Finnish entry into the EU and raising of their import duties.</p>
<p>The quota was agreed by the EU cereals management committee on February 27.</p>
<p>--Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
